    "body": "I like the direction of this fix. Ultimately, it's a dummy run problem. It's creating an invalid combination of `num_tokens` and `num_reqs` that would never be scheduled in practice. However, I think the fix can be scoped further to just `_dummy_run`. It has all the information it needs to re-derive a valid `num_reqs` for the given speculator. For example:\n\n```\nnum_reqs = min(num_tokens, self.max_num_reqs)\nif uniform_decode:\n    ...\nelif not skip_attn and self.speculator is not None:\n    num_reqs = min(\n        num_reqs, self.max_num_tokens // self.speculator.num_query_per_req\n    )\n```\n\nWhat are your thoughts on this approach instead?",
